\newpage
\begin{verbatim}

% TRANSFORMATION TVerbLeft
< m1: I1::CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
                [I2:mu1,
                 I3:mu2,
                 predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                        [I6:mu6,
                         rel1/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu3],
                         I4:mu4
                        ],
                 mu5
                ]
>

< m : I1::CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
                [I2:mu1,
                 auxrel/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu3],
                 I3:mu2,
                 predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                        [I6:mu6,
                         I4:mu4],
                 mu5
                ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: CLAUSErec1.finiteness = finite
       I2: NOT EXIST (mu1, [ I21:rel2/..])
           I21: rel2 IN AUX_postauxAdvRels OR rel2 = negrel
       I3: ALL (mu2, I31:rel3/..)
           I31: rel3 IN AUX_postauxAdvRels OR rel3 = negrel
       I4: NOT EXIST (mu4, [ I41:rel4/..])
           I41: rel4 IN AUX_beginVPAdvRels
       I6: ALL (mu6, I61:rel6/..)
           I61: rel6 IN AUX_beginVPAdvRels
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: VERBrec1.subc = doaux AND
              rel1 = auxrel
          A1: @

          C2: VERBrec1.subc = modalverb AND
              rel1 = auxrel
          A2: @

          C3: VERBrec1.subc = haveVerb AND
              rel1 = auxrel
          A3: @

          C4: VERBrec1.subc = beVerb AND
              rel1 = progauxrel
          A4: @

          C5: VERBrec1.subc = beVerb AND
              CLAUSErec1.voice = passive AND
              rel1 = passauxrel
          A5: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: VERBrec1.subc = doaux
          A1: rel1 := auxrel

          C2: VERBrec1.subc = modalverb 
          A2: rel1 := auxrel

          C3: VERBrec1.subc = haveVerb
          A3: rel1 := auxrel

          C4: VERBrec1.subc = beVerb 
          A4: rel1 := progauxrel

          C5: VERBrec1.subc = beVerb AND
              CLAUSErec1.voice = passive
          A5: rel1 := passauxrel
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TVerbLeft
\item[* relevant examples:] \mbox{}\\
\begin{enumerate}
\item CA-pair 1: He do [have a book], He do [see it], He do [be a nuisance]
(`Do' will be removed later for main verbs like `be' and in analysis for `have'
)
\item CA-pair 2: He can [do it], He may not [do it]
\item CA-pair 3: He have [done it]
\item CA-pair 4: He be [doing it]
\item CA-pair 5: It be [done]
\end{enumerate}
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) english
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_VerbLeft
\item[* date of creation:] 19-FEB-1988
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] TNoVerbLeft
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 15/02/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
Adapted I2 and I3 to allow for negrels. This is needed because some 010 modals 
accept an embedded sentence with a negrel in it. In RmodalComplSentSubst1 
this negrel is moved to the higher sentence, following any PostAuxAdvRels.
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] to provide a uniform structure for all finite clauses. Placement 
of the verb outside the VERBP is needed for subject-verb inversion, wh-shift 
etc.
